98
00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:45.691
Here's the prompt we can use, which
is. We're going to use an LLM

99
00:05:45.691 --> 00:05:49.919
and tell it to be an assistant that
evaluates how well the

100
00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:52.737
customer service agent answers
a user question by

101
00:05:52.737 --> 00:05:55.555
comparing the response, that was
the automatically generated

102
00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:58.021
one, to the
ideal (expert) human written

103
00:05:58.021 --> 00:05:58.374
response.

104
00:05:58.935 --> 00:06:03.894
So we're going to give it the data, which
is what was the customer request, what

105
00:06:03.894 --> 00:06:07.304
is the expert written ideal response,
and then what did our

106
00:06:07.304 --> 00:06:08.234
LLM actually output.

